{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>What will You give me.</b> In this world." "<b>Childless.</b> That I have no son to fill my place in the management of my property, as it says (Jeremiah 22:30): כִּתְבוּ אֶת הָאִישׁ הַזֶּה עֲרִירִי כִּי לֹא יִצְלַח מִזַּרְעוֹ אִישׁ יוֹשֵׁב עַל כִּסֵּא דָוִד — \"Record this man as childless, for no man of his seed shall succeed to the throne of David.\"" "<b>And the son of the steward of my house is Eliezer of Damascus.</b> For he is a slave, not known by his own name, but only by the name of his city. And there is no doubt that the actions of a slave in managing the household and property — which proceed from fear — differ greatly from the actions of a son in managing them — which proceed from love."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:11.671254246Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}